# Caching & Sync

## Purpose

Preserve the cache-first / stale-while-revalidate experience on lists and dashboards.

## When Applied

Touching cache infra or any list/dashboard/home data path.

## Requirements

- Building blocks: Hive (`LocalCacheStore`) snapshots, in-memory TTL cache, `StreamRepository<T>` (stream + TTL + dedupe + auto-refresh), `MemberDataSync` / prefetch services.
- Emit cached data first, then refresh.
- After mutations affecting member home/booking/sessions, invalidate via existing sync helpers — do not build a parallel cache bus.
- Prefer `unawaited(...)` for non-blocking cache writes (match existing style).
- See [`docs/caching-and-sync.md`](../../../docs/caching-and-sync.md).

## Examples

- New live admin list → extend `StreamRepository<T>` and reuse its TTL/dedupe.

## Anti-patterns

- Removing TTL/stream caching while "simplifying" a repository (unless asked).
- A second, ad-hoc cache/invalidation mechanism alongside `MemberDataSync`.

## Common Mistakes

- Awaiting cache writes on the UI path and adding latency.
- Mutating data without invalidating the affected cache keys.
